= Biological database — Simple =

A biological database organizes biological data so researchers and software can find and use it. Entries can contain sequences, annotations, structures, variants, metadata, and links. A database record can include predictions or submitted claims, not only experimentally proven facts.

'''Important boundary:''' biological database ≠ flat file collection.

